///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
/*			
	Copyright © 2006 DVY_Vehicle Rigger. All rights reserved davvey@ntlworld.com

						 - DVY_VehicleRigger -
						 
///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
				
	This set of scripts will build a Vehicle Rig for wheel rotation, suspension
	and steering. Also it will rig Doors, Front Hood (Bonnet), Rear Trunk (Boot) or
	or Rear Tailgate or Split Tailgate or Rear Left and Right Doors.
	This script is called by the GUI DVY_Vehicle Rigger.mel

	This script currently has minimsl error checking if you find it useful please
	let me know and I will rewrite it with full error checking.
	
	This script was written to demonstrate the use of Utility nodes to replace
	expressions for vehicle control etc.
	
	I am currently working on building a full suite of scripts to allow rigging
	of all the various parts of any wheeled vehicle. The intention is to build a
	set of "modular" scripts to allow rigging oif individual parts and or a fullly
	rigged vehicle.
	
	Directions:
	
	Source and run DVY_Vehicle Rigger.mel, use default values is you have named them 
	as shown or selct each item in turn and load required field. Also you can type names
	in the field as required. Script will error out if not all items are found.
	Once all fields correct press "Rig Vehicle" button. 
	
	Each Tab must be initialized by selecting the relevant CheckBox on the first Tab.
	To set up the Doors and Hood Section, select the required items using the check
	boxes, then select the items or use default values (same as wheel section method).
	Once all field completed press the "Set Hinge Position" Button on that Tab.
	Repeat for Hood etc Tab if required , then adjust position of the Blue Spheres to
	the exact position you want the Hinge point to be. Then adjust the Red Spheres to
	the `Handle` position for item item. The Blue Spheres can be Translated and Rotated,
	the Red just Translated. The Red handle sphere is used to set the angle of rotation
	of the Hinge. The limit of opening angle is 110 degrees but this can be changed 
	using the Controllers `Y` Translate Axis limits in the Attribute Editor
	
	The Window Spheres (green and Yellow) carry out a similar function but are used
	to set up a sliding action to simulate Window opening.
	
	Structure of intial Vehicle is as follows :-
	
	Vehicle Top Node
	 |___
		|
		|___BodyShell Group
			|
		  	|_____BodyWork_Group 
		  	|	  |
		  	|	  |__Door_GrpN_1
			|	  |	 |
		  	|	  |	 |__LfFr_Door_GrpN_1
			|	  |	 |__RtFr_Door_GrpN_1
			|	  |	 |__LfRr_Door_GrpN_1
			|	  |	 |__RtRr_Door_GrpN_1 
			|	  |
			|	  |__Fr_Hood_GrpN_1
			|	  |__Rr_Trunk_GrpN_1 or Rr_Tailgate_GrpN_1 
			|	  |
			|	  |					 or	(Rr_TopTailgate_GrpN_1
			|	  |						 Rr_BotTailgate_GrpN_1)
			|	  |
			|	  |					 or (LfRr_Tailgate_GrpN_1
			|	  |						 RtRr_TailDoor_GrpN_1)
			|	  |
			|	  |
			|	  |__Remaining Chassis parts(contains all geometry except Wheels.
			|
		  	|___Wheels Grp_1 
			  	|___
					|Fr_Wheels_Grp_1
					|	|
					|	|__ LfFr_Wheel_Grp_1	(Wheel Group Naming must follow
					|	|__ RtFr_Wheel_Grp_1	  this structure i.e 
					|	|__ LfFr_Wheel_Grp_2	  LfFr_Wheel_Grp_1,  LfFr_Wheel _Grp_2
					|	|__ RtFr_Wheel_Grp_2	  order is not important within each of
					|							  the Group Nodes.)
					|Rr_Wheels_Grp_1
						|
						|__ LfRr_Wheel_Grp_1
						|__ RtRr_Wheel_Grp_1
						|__ LfRr_Wheel_Grp_2
						|__ RtRr_Wheel_Grp_2	
			
			
	Basic Procedure:
		Main procedure uses a $GroupV_A to store main groups from GUI and 
		build a rig of joints with locators as reuired.
		Joints are constrained to individual locators.
		Also some locators are constrained to individual joints.
		
		Wheels can be individually controlled based on distnace moved or set
		to spin based on time (see help file for more info).
		
		There are 4 Main "Rig Contollers" plus auxillary Controllers.
		
		Rig_ControllerN_1 :-
		
			Controls movement and rotation of main vehicle.
			Also houses attributes for setting range of suspension travel
			using attribute Piston Range. Also there are also individual
			range settings for each wheel(not active yet).
		
		Steering_ControllerN_1 
		
			Controls steering for Front and Rear Wheels. The front steering
			is active by default, to activate Rear steering set "Rr Steer"
			to On. Setting the "Fr Steer Ratio" and "Rr Steer Ratios" to a 
			negative value will reverse direction of rotation.
			Set "Fr Steer to Off will set vehicle to have rerar steering.
			The ratio can be set anywhere between -1 and 1, this will
			reduce effect of rotation to simulat the Rear wheel steer you
			now see on some high performance cars.
		
		Bank_ControllerN_1
		
			This will Bank the Vehicle by a mavximum of 5 degrees in both 
			X and Z +/- axis and still allow full susupension control.
			The maximum range can be altered in the attribute editor by adjusting
			the X and Z axis rotate limits.
			
		VehicleTilt_ControllerN_1
		
			This will tilt the Chassis group as reguired. Also each indiviual
			Wheel can be moved up and down by moving each wheel Group Ground 
			Locator to simulate ground variations.
			
			Also if Doors and Hand and TRunk Options are selected then there will
			be individual controllers for each Door or BodyShell Section. Plus
			individual controllers for each opening window (sliding open).
			
		Auxillary Controllers 
			(For Door, Window, Front Hood and Rear Runk or Tailgate)
			
			The Auxillary Controllers are set up for each individual section i.e.
			Left Front passenger Door, Right Front Passenger Door. If required
			a Window Controller will be added as required. The controls are set
			up so that transaltion in the Horizontal direction will drive the
			opening or closing by rotation of the relevant section or item.
			The Window Contollers work in the Vertical direction and open the
			window by a sliding action.
	
		Floor Control

			There is an option to set up an automatic wheel control for each
			wheel by setting up a Geometry Constaint to a "Ground Plane".
			This has an auto ON/OFF setup which releases the wheels once car
			leaves the ground a distance greater than suspension travel.
			
		Motion Path
		
			To setup Vehicle to Motion Path. Select Rig_Controller and Motion
			Path. This will set up and parent a locator under Vehicle Top Node
			and constrain the Rig Controls to the motion path via the locator.
			The remain controls will operate as usual and wheels will either 
			auto rotate based on movement or based on wheel spin settings
			
*/	
	
//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
//					DVY_VehicleRigger Procedure
//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////

// DVY_VehicleRigger;
	
//============================================================================
//	GLOBAL VARIABLES
//============================================================================
	global int $DVYDebug;

// Integer Flag that allows print statements to be output to
// message field for tracking purposes.
		
//============================================================================

	
global proc DVY_VehicleRigger()
{
	global int $DVYDebug;
	global string $GroupV_A[]; clear $GroupV_A; 
	global string $DVY_VehName;
	global string $DVYSide ="NA";	global string $DVYPos ="NA"; 	global string $DVYLocn ="NA";

	global string $DVYList = "VehicleGroupTextScrollList";
	global string $DVYVehicleList[]; clear $DVYVehicleList;
	global float $DVYdata[], $DVYGUIData[]; clear $DVYGUIData;
	
//============================================================================
	string $DVYSel[];

	string $SpringSetup;		// Spring Tab Name
	string $VehicleOptions;		// Vehicle location Tab Nmae.
	string $TempSel;	int $DVYName = 0; 	string $Named[];	string $Name;
//============================================================================
	
	//	Check for any "Window History" and delete if it exists.
//	 	if (`windowPref -exists DVY_VehiclRigWindow`) windowPref -r DVY_VehiclRigWindow;
//			windowPref -edit -topLeftCorner 250 700 -widthHeight 315 600 DVY_VehicleRigWindow;
	
	//Check for multiple similar windows.
		if (`window -q -ex DVY_VehicleRigWindow`) deleteUI DVY_VehicleRigWindow; 
		if (`windowPref -q -ex DVY_VehicleRigWindow`) {windowPref -remove DVY_VehicleRigWindow;}
	//Build window.
		window -w 875 -h 780 -tlc 80 350 -rtf 1 -s 1 -title "Davvey's Vehicle Rigger v1.52" DVY_VehicleRigWindow;
	
	//Build 'Edit' menu.
		global string $Path;
		$Path = `internalVar -uad`;
		$Path = ($Path + "Documentation" + "\/Davveys_Rig_Help_File.pdf");
//		print ("Path is " + $Path + "\n");
		
	string $menuBarLayout = `menuBarLayout`;
		menu -label "File"; 
 			menuItem -label "Close" -command "deleteUI DVY_VehicleRigWindow";		
		menu -label "Help"; 
	// 		menuItem -label "SetUp Help" -command "DVY_HelpWin";
			menuItem -label "SetUp Help" -command "system(\"load \" + $Path)";
			
		menu -label "About"; 
	 		menuItem -label "About Davvey's Rig" -command " DVY_AboutWin;";	
			
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//	
//							End of MenuBar Panel Layout
//
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
				
	string $PaneLayout = `paneLayout -height 780 -paneSize 1 25 100 -configuration "vertical2" "DVY_Rig_PaneLayout"`;
			
//++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
//	
//				Start Of Outliner Panel Layout to allow selection of Vehicle Parts
//
//++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++	
// THIS IS THE OUTLINER PANEL
	
	string $OutlinerFrame = `frameLayout -borderStyle "etchedOut" -collapsable false 
										 -label "DVY_Outliner PanelInfo" -labelVisible false` ;
	
	string $panel = `outlinerPanel -menuBarVisible false`;
		string $outliner = `outlinerPanel -query -outlinerEditor $panel`;
			outlinerEditor -edit
				-mainListConnection "worldList" 
				-selectionConnection "modelList" 
				-showShapes false
				-showAttributes false
				-showConnected false
				-showAnimCurvesOnly false
				-autoExpand false
				-showDagOnly true
				-ignoreDagHierarchy false
				-expandConnections false
				-showCompounds false
				-showNumericAttrsOnly false
				-highlightActive true
				-autoSelectNewObjects false
				-doNotSelectNewObjects false
				-transmitFilters false
				-showSetMembers false
				-setFilter DefaultGeometryFilter
			$outliner;
			
		setParent..;
	setParent..;
	
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//	
//							End of Outliner Panel Layout
//
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

			
//++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
//	
//						Start Of RigPane Layout to hold Vehicle Name and Info
//
//+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++	
//	Define a Pane Layout for all the Rigging Tabs and Buttons.
	
	string $RigPaneLayout = `paneLayout -paneSize 1 100 17 -paneSize 3 100 27 -configuration "horizontal3" "RigPane"`;	
		
// Create Vehicle Name Pane
		
	string $VehicleN = `columnLayout -cat "both" 2 -cal "center" -adjustableColumn true "VehicleNamePanel:"`;

	
	iconTextStaticLabel -w 360 -h 50 -st "iconOnly" -i1 "DavveyLogo.xpm" VIMage ;		

// Title and Info Section for the "Initial Setup" tab. 
		
		text -height 2 -label " " ;	//Spacer
		separator -height 5 -style "double" ;
		text -bgc .5 .5 1 -height 20 -align "center" -font "boldLabelFont" -label "Davvey's Vehicle Rigger.";
		
//		text -bgc .5 .5 1 -height 20 -align "center" -font "boldLabelFont" -label "Setup Vehicle Group Options Setup.";
		separator -height 5 -style "double";
		text -height 2 -label " " ;	//Spacer
		
	rowColumnLayout -nc 3 -cw 1 300 -cat 1 "both" 5 -cal 1 "center"
						  -cw 2 300 -cat 2 "both" 5 -cal 2 "center" ;
	
		textField -text "Davveys_Car_" -ann "Enter Vehicle Name and Press button" VehicleGrpNTextField;
		textField -text " " -editable false VehicleGrpNameTextField;
			
	setParent..;	
	
	rowColumnLayout -nc 1 -cw 1 610 -cat 1 "both" 50 -cal 1 "center" "VehicleNameC";	
	
		text -height 2 -label " ";	
		button -bgc 0.7 1 0.7 -label "Enter Vehicle Name  >>"
				-command "$TempSel[0] = `textField -q -tx VehicleGrpNTextField`;\ $DVY_VehName = $TempSel[0];\ textField -edit -text $TempSel[0] VehicleGrpNameTextField;";
		text -height 2 -label " ";	
		
	setParent $RigPaneLayout;	
	
//++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
//	
//						Start Of Tab Layout to hold Vehicle Tab Layouts
//
//+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++	
	global string $Tabs, $Tab01, $Tab02, $Tab03, $Tab04, $Tab05, $Tab06;
		
	$Tabs = `tabLayout -innerMarginWidth 1 -innerMarginHeight 1	 "TabLayout"`;
		
//++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
//	
//							Start of Setup and Info Tab
//
//+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++			
	global string $BodyShellFrame, $BodyShellFrameC, $SetupInfoFrameC, $SetupHelpFrameC;
	
	$Tab01 = `columnLayout -adjustableColumn true -cat "both" 1 "Setup"`;	

	rowColumnLayout -nc 1 -cw 1 610 -cat 1 "both" 2 -cal 1 "center" "VehicleList2";	
		
		separator -h 10 -style "double";
			
// Startof BodyShell "Checkbox" Section. If not selected then no Options will be setup.

	checkBoxGrp -numberOfCheckBoxes 4 -labelArray4 "Wheels" "Front and Rear Doors" "Hood and Trunk" "Ancillaries"
		-enable1 true -enable2 false -enable3 false -enable4 false 
		-label "Sections to Setup:- " 
		-cw 1 110 -cal 1 "right" 
		-cw 2 65 -cal 2 "left"
		-cw 3 130 -cal 3 "left"
		-cw 4 170 -cal 4 "left"
		-cw 5 170 -cal 4 "left"
			
			-onCommand1 "frameLayout -edit -enable true -vis true -collapse false $BodyShellFrame; frameLayout -edit -collapse true $SetupInfoFrameC; frameLayout -edit -collapse true $SetupHelpFrameC; checkBoxGrp -edit -enable2 true SetUpOptionsCheck; checkBoxGrp -edit -enable3 true SetUpOptionsCheck;"
						 
			-onCommand2 "columnLayout -edit -enable true $Tab03;"
						  
			-onCommand3 "columnLayout -edit -enable true $Tab04; checkBoxGrp -edit -enable false HoodsOptionsCheck;"		
						 
			-onCommand4 "columnLayout -edit -enable false $Tab05;"
					
			-offCommand1 "frameLayout -edit -enable false -vis false -collapse false $BodyShellFrame; frameLayout -edit -collapse false $SetupInfoFrameC; frameLayout -edit -collapse false $SetupHelpFrameC; checkBoxGrp -edit -enable2 false SetUpOptionsCheck; checkBoxGrp -edit -enable3 false SetUpOptionsCheck;"
						  
			-offCommand2 "columnLayout -edit -enable false $Tab03;"
			
			-offCommand3 "columnLayout -edit -enable false $Tab04;"
			
			-offCommand4 "columnLayout -edit -enable false $Tab05;"
			
		SetUpOptionsCheck;

// End of BodyShell "Checkbox" Section. If not selected then no Options will be setup.
//***********************************************************************************	
// Create a Frame Layout to hold Setup Info etc.
	string $SetupInfoFrame = `frameLayout -borderStyle "etchedOut" -collapsable false
										  -label "Setup Info" -labelVisible false` ;
				
// Create a Layout for Title Section of the Setup Frame.
	string $SetupInfoColumn = `columnLayout -adjustableColumn true -cat "both" 2 "SetupInfoColumn"`;	

// Create a collapsible frame layout
	string $SetupInfoFrameC = `	frameLayout -collapsable true -collapse false -label "  Info"` ;	
		
// Create a collapsable Frame for Setup Info.
	string $SetupInfoColumnC = `columnLayout -adjustableColumn true -cat "both" 2 "SetupInfoColumnC"`;	

		separator -h 10 -style "double";
			text -bgc 1 1 .85 -height 5 -label "" ;	//Space
			text -bgc 1 1 .85 -align "left" -label
				" This a copy of the GUI I am building for Vehicle Rigging. Not all sections are currently available. Sections will be greyed out";
			text -bgc 1 1 .85 -align "left" 
				-label " but visible for comments and to give an idea of what I am hoping to eventually end up with as a Vehicle Rigging script pack.";
			text -bgc 1 1 .85 -align "left" 
				-label " The UI will only run the sections that are currently scripted with the accompanying scripts included. These are based on the ";
			text -bgc 1 1 .85 -align "left" 
				-label " original scripts contained in `Davvey's Vehicle Rigging`. Each Field is disabled until the prevous field has been 'Intialized'.";
			text -bgc 1 1 .85 -align "left" -label " I have tried to make the 'Rigging Setup' flow in a logical form.\n";
			separator -bgc 1 1 .85 -height 5 -style "double";
			text -bgc 1 1 .85 -height 5 -label "" ;	//Spacer
			text -bgc 1 1 .85 -align "left" -font "boldLabelFont" -label " So any comments good or bad please let me know. Also if you like it please rate the Script Pack at";
			text -bgc 1 1 .85 -align "left" -font "boldLabelFont" -label " http://highend3d.com/maya/downloads/mel_scripts/animation/4109.html";
			text -bgc 1 1 .85 -align "left" -font "boldLabelFont" -label " Please contact me at Davvey@ntlworld.com with feedback or suggestions. thanks and enjoy.";
			text -bgc 1 1 .85 -height 5 -label "" ;	//Spacer
		separator -height 5 -style "double";
